{"name":"Habañero Chile","hex":"#b8473d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"habañero","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(hypercorrect) Nonstandard form of habanero."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haba%C3%B1ero"},{"term":"chile","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of chili."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Pronunciation spelling of child, representing Southern US and African-American Vernacular English."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chile"}],"entries":[{"title":"Habanero","blocks":[{"text":"The habanero is a pungent cultivar of Capsicum chinense chili pepper. Unripe habaneros are green, and they color as they mature. The most common color variants are orange and red, but the fruit may also be white, brown, yellow, green, or purple. Typically, a ripe habanero is 2–6 centimetres long. Habanero chilis are very hot, rated 100,000–350,000 on the Scoville scale. The habanero's heat, flavor, and floral aroma make it a common ingredient in hot sauces and other spicy foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Habanero_closeup_edit2.jpg/330px-Habanero_closeup_edit2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habanero","wikidata":"Q764375"},{"title":"Chile","blocks":[{"text":"Chile, officially the Republic of Chile, is a country in the Southern Cone of southwestern South America. It is the southernmost country in the world and the closest to Antarctica, extending along a narrow strip of land between the Andes Mountains and the Pacific Ocean. According to the 2024 census, Chile had an enumerated population of 18.5 million. The country covers a territorial area of 756,102 square kilometers (291,933 sq mi), sharing borders with Peru to the north, Bolivia to the northeast, Argentina to the east, and the Drake Passage to the south. It also administers several Pacific islands, including Juan Fernández, Isla Salas y Gómez, Desventuradas, and Easter Island, and claims about 1,250,000 square kilometers (480,000 sq mi) of Antarctica as the Chilean Antarctic Territory. The capital and largest city is Santiago, and the official and national language is Spanish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Flag_of_Chile.svg/330px-Flag_of_Chile.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chile","wikidata":"Q298"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/ExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG/500px-ExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/ExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG/1280px-ExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/ExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG/500px-ExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Habanero hot sauce from Flor de Lirio, an Indigenous cooperative in Peto Municipality, Yucatán","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Habanero_cut_in_half_on_a_blue_plate.jpg/500px-Habanero_cut_in_half_on_a_blue_plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Habanero_cut_in_half_on_a_blue_plate.jpg/1280px-Habanero_cut_in_half_on_a_blue_plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Habanero_cut_in_half_on_a_blue_plate.jpg/500px-Habanero_cut_in_half_on_a_blue_plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A habanero peppe